course: dictionary
lesson: 14450
title: The Paralympic Games
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «The Paralympics are held every four years, after the Olympic Games.» Read the clues: it is a big sports event, it happens every four years, and it comes just after the Olympics. So the Paralympics is an international sports competition.
explain: «Mia watched wheelchair basketball at the Paralympics and cheered for every goal.» The sport and the cheering tell you it is a sporting event where disabled athletes compete at a high level.
explain: «Her brother dreams of becoming a Paralympian one day.» A Paralympian is an athlete who competes at the Paralympics. Check it by swapping in «an athlete who competes» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Paralympics is a noun: the Paralympics, or the Paralympic Games.
fact: Paralympic is an adjective, as in «a Paralympic champion».
fact: The Paralympics is a big international sports competition for athletes with disabilities.
fact: It is held after the Olympic Games, every four years.
fact: Sports at the Paralympics include wheelchair basketball, blind football, boccia and para swimming.
exercise: «The Paralympics are held every four years, after the Olympic Games.» What are the Paralympics? | *A big international sports competition for athletes with disabilities | A school test in maths | A type of bread served at the Olympic village
exercise: Which of these is a sport played at the Paralympics? | *Wheelchair basketball | Spelling bee | Pancake racing | Ballet
exercise: «Her brother dreams of becoming a Paralympian one day.» What is a Paralympian? | A coach who sells medals | *An athlete who competes at the Paralympics | A fan who only watches from home | A PE teacher who runs the school sports day
test: When are the Paralympics held, compared with the Olympic Games? | Never at the same time as any other event | *Just after them | On the same day, every year | Just before them
test: Which word in «a Paralympic champion» is the adjective? | a | *Paralympic | Champion
exam: How often are the Summer and Winter Paralympics held? | *Every four years | Every week | Every ten years | Every year
